            <div xml:id="d587">

                <pb facs="0808" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/2075</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4171</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-16">December 16, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        23.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on Tuesday
                    afternoon, by appointment, I visited President Cárdenas at his home. I was
                    accompanied by Mr. Pierre de L. Boal, Counselor of the Embassy. I had sought the
                    appointment before going to the United States on leave in order to discuss with
                    him the agrarian dotations of land belonging <pb facs="0809" n="710"
                        xml:id="pg710"/> to Americans and the new expropriation law, about which
                    instructions had been received from the Department, and one or two other
                    subjects in which our country is interested. We talked, the President at length
                    discussing the subjects which I presented, and about which I had told him on a
                    former visit that my countrymen and my government were greatly perturbed. At my
                    request Mr. Boal has prepared a summary of the interview which is appended
                    hereto.</p>
                <p>I will be in Washington on Monday and will discuss the subjects touched upon in
                    the interview with President Cárdenas and will try to give the background of the
                    situation in Mexico.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d587-a1.xml" xpointer="d587-a1"/>
            </div>
